   "url": "https://wristfit.feijoalabs.com/smartwatch-small-wrists.html",
   "title": "Smartwatches for small wrists: the models that fit",
   "snippet": "",
   "text": "Smartwatches for small wrists: the models that fit \n Smartwatches for small wrists, by the numbers\n A small wrist kills smartwatches two ways: the case overhangs the wrist edges, and the band bottoms out at its smallest setting before it is snug [4] [7] . Both failures are checkable before you buy, with numbers the manufacturers publish. This page lists the models that actually fit small wrists with their case dimensions, weights, and official band minimums, and the two checks that decide fit. It is the model-picking companion to our step-by-step smartwatch sizing guide and the full smartwatch case-size table .\n Three things to know before shopping. \n The band minimum, not the case size, decides fit on small wrists: Garmin's Lily 2 fits from 110mm, Apple's S/M bands from 130mm, Versa 4 small bands from 130mm [1] [5] [6] .\n The smallest true smartwatches are genuinely small: Lily 2 is 35.4 x 35.4 x 10.1mm and 24g [1] [2] .\n Under 150mm circumference, skip 44mm-class cases entirely; 42mm+ overhangs and the bands often start at 140mm or higher [4] [7] .\n The small-wrist smartwatch table\n Manufacturer-published dimensions and wrist-fit figures, each cross-checked against at least two sources:\n Model Case (mm) Weight Official wrist fit Band width \n Garmin Lily 2 / Classic 35.4 x 35.4 x 10.1 24g 110-175mm 14mm \n Garmin Lily 2 Active 38 x 38 x 11 28g 110-175mm class 14mm \n Apple Watch SE / Series, 40mm class ~40 x 36 x 10.7 ~27-31g S/M band from 130mm proprietary \n Samsung Galaxy Watch, 40mm 40.4 x 40.4 x 9.7 (Watch7) ~28-31g S/M band ~130-190mm 20mm \n Fitbit Versa 4 family, small band 40.5 x 40.5 x 11.2 ~38g with band S band 130-178mm proprietary \n Fitbit Luxe (tracker) slim steel tracker ~34g S band 140-180mm proprietary \n Fitbit Inspire 3 (tracker) 39.3 x 18.6 x 11.75 body 17.7g S band 130-190mm proprietary \n Sources: Garmin Lily 2 dimensions and 110-175mm wrist range from Garmin's published specs as transcribed by fitness-tracker-test.info and recoveryforathletes.com [1] [2] ; Apple and Galaxy band ranges from the manufacturer tables on our Apple band size and smartwatch sizing pages, cross-checked against MacRumors' band guide [5] ; numbered Apple loop sizes on our Solo Loop sizing chart ; Versa 4 small-band 130-178mm from Fitbit's official chart on our Versa band page [6] ; Luxe 140-180mm and Inspire 3 130-190mm small-band figures from the Fitbit Luxe manual (140-180mm S band) and Google Store's Inspire 3 spec page (130-190mm small) [3] [8] . Inspire 3 body is 39.32 x 18.6 x 11.75mm per Google Store [8] .\n Why the Lily 2 is the floor\n Garmin built the Lily line for exactly this problem: a 35.4mm case (38mm on the Active version with built-in GPS), 10.1mm thick, 24g with strap, on 14mm quick-release bands, fitting wrists from 110mm circumference [1] [2] . Nothing else that runs a real app ecosystem goes lower. The trade-offs are honest: a monochrome patterned-lens display, connected GPS only on the base model, and no ECG; the Lily 2 Active adds GPS and buttons in the larger 38mm case at 28g [2] . Band ecosystem note: the 14mm lug width is narrower than Garmin's QuickFit standard elsewhere, so check our Garmin band size page before buying spares.\n The two checks before you buy any smartwatch\n Check 1: the band minimum. Find the manufacturer's \"fits wrists\" figure for the band that ships with the case you chose. Apple publishes S/M and M/L ranges per band type (S/M roughly 130-180mm) [5] ; Samsung quotes S/M and M/L bands around 130-190 and 145-205mm rather than per-case figures [6] ; Fitbit prints S/L ranges on the box (Versa 4 small: 130-178mm) [6] . If your wrist is below the small band's floor, the watch will never be snug, and a loose smartwatch is not just uncomfortable: gaps under the sensor degrade heart-rate accuracy [4] .\n Check 2: overhang. Case width plus lugs must not exceed your wrist width, the flat top of your wrist. Measure your wrist circumference (60 seconds, no tools, on our how to measure page), convert to wrist width with the calculator , and compare against the case's longer dimension. Round 40mm cases are 40.4mm wide (Galaxy Watch7) [6] ; squarish Apple cases run about 40 x 36mm, which is why they wear smaller than the number suggests. The full method, with the mistake list, is in our sizing guide's overhang check .\n What to skip on a small wrist\n 44mm and 46mm cases (Galaxy Watch 44, Apple 44/46mm, Venu 3 45mm): overhang plus bands that often start at 145mm [6] [7] .\n Ultra-class 49mm watches: 130-210mm band range aside, the case is a brick on a sub-150mm wrist [6] .\n \"One size\" bands with no published minimum: if the maker will not print the floor, assume it is too high [7] .\n If the watch you want is borderline, the band can be fixed after the fact (smaller aftermarket bands, or the elastic and nylon options on our materials page ), but the case cannot. When both sizes of a model exist, this page's numbers plus the calculator decide: see how to choose between the two sizes .\n Related pages\n Smartwatch sizing guide : the four-step measure-and-check process\n Smartwatch case sizes : full dimensions and wrist-fit table by model\n Watch case size by wrist : the traditional-watch version of this chart\n Garmin band sizes : 14mm Lily bands vs QuickFit, by model\n Sources\n Fitness Tracker Test, Garmin Lily 2 review spec table (35.4 x 35.4 x 10.1mm, 24g with strap, 14mm band, Gorilla Glass 3, monochrome display) and recoveryforathletes.com Garmin Lily 2 product page (fits wrist circumference 110-175mm, 24.4g, 5 ATM): fitness-tracker-test.info , recoveryforathletes.com \n Garmin Rumors wiki, Lily 2 and Lily Series pages (Lily 2 Classic 35.4mm aluminum / Lily 2 Active 38 x 38 x 11mm with built-in GPS, 24g / 28g with band, 14mm standard quick-release bands, small-form-factor positioning, monochrome patterned lens): wiki.garminrumors.com \n Fitbit Luxe user manual, band size table (small band fits 140-180mm, large 180-220mm circumference): Fitbit Luxe manual (PDF) \n TheWearify, fitness tracker fit and placement guides (band-minimum method, 4.3 in floor example, models to avoid on small wrists, sensor-contact accuracy argument for snug fit): thewearify.com \n Apple Watch S/M vs M/L band ranges and Solo Loop sizing, as documented on our Apple Watch band size page from Apple's live band pages transcribed by MacRumors: wristfit.feijoalabs.com/apple-watch-band-size.html \n Our verified smartwatch case-size table (Apple 40/42mm and Ultra 2 dimensions and wrist fits, Galaxy Watch7 40.4mm with S/M ~130-190 and M/L ~145-205mm bands, Versa 4 40.5mm S band 130-178mm, Venu 3S 110-175mm), built from manufacturer spec pages and independent reviews: wristfit.feijoalabs.com/smartwatch-sizing.html and fitbit-versa-band-size.html \n TheWearify small-wrist model guidance (cases under 41mm for small wrists, band minimums 5.5-6.0 in on 44mm-class models failing sub-5.5 in wrists, one-size band skepticism): thewearify.com \n Google Store, Fitbit Inspire 3 technical specifications (body 39.32 x 18.6 x 11.75mm, 17.69g, small band fits 130-190mm, large 160-220mm): store.google.com",
